The sum carries the injection. The sum of the two injections equals the injection of the sum subsystem, so both relations hold of a pair of neighbourhoods precisely when the source lies in the smaller sum, the target lies in the larger sum, and the source is included in the target.

Every neighbourhood of the smaller sum is included in the master of the larger sum, by the master equality on the master neighbourhood and by the tagged embeddings of the factor inclusions. Extensionality then matches a master step by that inclusion and a left or right tagged step by the tagged inclusion of the corresponding factor. Conversely a master target is the master case. A left target against the master would place the empty string in a tag, a left target against a right source is a cross-tag inclusion, and a left target against a left source is the factor inclusion. The right-target cases are the symmetric three.
